Error in if (numThresholdMarker[i] == 1) lavaanParTable <- fixParTable(lavaanParTable,  :
  missing value where TRUE/FALSE needed

In addition: Warning message:
In lav_samplestats_from_data(lavdata = lavdata, missing = lavoptions$missing,  :
  lavaan WARNING: 41 bivariate tables have empty cells; to see them, use:
                  lavInspect(fit, "zero.cell.tables")

Script
model = "

f4 =~ f1 + f2 + f3

f1 =~ i1 + i2 + i3
f2 =~ i4 + i5
f3 =~ i6 + i7
"

# Error, missing value, and warning, empty cells
measurementInvarianceCat(model, data, group="g", estimator="WLSMV")

# Warning, empty cells (proceeds without errors or warnings if indicators are made to be integer variables)

measurementInvariance(model, data, group="g", estimator="WLSMV")

# Error, does not converge (proceeds without errors or warnings if indicators are made to be integer variables)
measurementInvariance(model, data, group="g", estimator="MLR")

# Error, empty categories
measurementInvarianceCat(model, data, group="h", estimator="WLSMV")

# Error, does not converge (proceeds with warnings of negative variances if indicators are made to be integer variables)
measurementInvariance(model, data, group="h", estimator="WLSMV")

# Error, does not converge (proceeds with warnings of negative variances if indicators are made to be integer variables)
measurementInvariance(model, data, group="h", estimator="MLR")

As you can see, I am also trying to test for invariance by another variable, "h", with many more levels, but these tests fail for different reasons, which I take to mean I simply cannot conclude invariance for that variable. In which case, I am planning on using a complex survey design (with the package lavaan.survey) to incorporate this. However, any recommendations would be appreciated.

