I need to perform a CFA where all indicators are 5-point Likert-type items. I want to report the outputs of:

1. parameterEstimates(mod, standardized = TRUE)

2. fitMeasures(fit)

3. reliability(fit)

Since thresholds are not symmetric, there is a significant difference in all outputs if I consider the analysis in two different datasets, one of them having indicators of type "numeric", and another having indicators of type "ordered". I would like you to confirm that the correct analysis must consider indicators of type "ordered". Moreover, as I understand, lavaan automatically selects the suitable estimator and other stuff; nevertheless, do you recommend to write additional options in the functions 1. - 3.?

